# Venture Atlas works without this file: the globes and all data are local.
# You only need a key for "Fetch latest" and "Add a company". Copy this file to .env and fill in ONE provider.

# ---- 1. AI provider (pick one) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude (Anthropic). Uses Anthropic's hosted web search, so no search key is needed.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ATLAS_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5            # optional; this is the default

# OpenAI
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ATLAS_MODEL=                           # required: a model that supports tool calling

# Google Gemini (through its OpenAI-compatible endpoint)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# ATLAS_MODEL=

# DeepSeek
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# ATLAS_MODEL=deepseek-chat              # optional; this is the default

# OpenRouter, Mistral, Groq
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# ATLAS_MODEL=

# Anything else that speaks the OpenAI chat-completions API (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, a company gateway…)
# ATLAS_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# ATLAS_API_KEY=                         # leave empty if the endpoint needs none
# ATLAS_MODEL=

# Force a provider when several keys are set: auto | anthropic | claude-code | openai | gemini | deepseek | openrouter | mistral | groq | custom
# ATLAS_PROVIDER=auto
# No key at all? If the Claude Code CLI is installed and logged in, it is used automatically.

# ---- 2. Web search (optional) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Providers other than Claude search through this server. Without a key it uses DuckDuckGo, which is free but rate-limited.
# For regular use add one of:
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
# BRAVE_API_KEY=
# SERPER_API_KEY=

# ---- 3. Behaviour (optional) ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Records whose every fact was confirmed on its source page are added straight to the atlas.
# Set to "off" to send everything to the review queue instead.
# ATLAS_AUTO_APPROVE=verified
# PORT=5173

# Limits per research run (defaults shown; an invalid value falls back to the default):
# ATLAS_MAX_SEARCHES=30
# ATLAS_MAX_FETCHES=45
# ATLAS_RUN_TIMEOUT_MIN=20
# ATLAS_MAX_SOURCES_PER_RECORD=10

# ---- 4. Phone app (optional) ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you install the app from GitHub Pages, list that address so it may call this server over Tailscale.
# Other machines on your own tailnet (https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net) are always allowed.
# ATLAS_APP_ORIGINS=https://<your-github-username>.github.io
# The server only answers to localhost, 127.0.0.1 and *.ts.net names. Add others here (e.g. a name on your home network):
# ATLAS_ALLOWED_HOSTS=atlas.lan
